1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,427
Away from home, or away from your PC?

2
00:00:03,427 --> 00:00:11,662
Cloud relay through Voltura lets your paired
phone, tablet, or another computer connect to
your Windows PC over the internet.

3
00:00:11,662 --> 00:00:16,327
You can use View PC screen to see and work on
that PC remotely.

4
00:00:16,327 --> 00:00:19,020
Let's set it up before you leave.

5
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:25,263
Keep the PC powered, connected to the internet,
and running Voltura Air.

6
00:00:25,263 --> 00:00:30,624
In its tray menu, open Keep awake and choose an
interval or Indefinitely.

7
00:00:30,624 --> 00:00:34,632
Keep screen on and simulated activity are
optional.

8
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:42,261
Keep awake prevents idle sleep while the host
runs; it cannot override manual Sleep or
closing a laptop lid.

9
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:47,087
In Voltura Air on your PC, open Connection.

10
00:00:47,087 --> 00:00:51,520
Under Connection method, select Cloud relay
through Voltura.

11
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:59,226
Both devices connect outward through Voltura,
so you don't need to open an incoming router
port or firewall exception.

12
00:00:59,226 --> 00:01:04,188
Leave Custom relay endpoint unchanged to use
Voltura's service.

13
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:07,776
Choose your screen relay quality.

14
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:11,487
Standard uses up to four megabits per second.

15
00:01:11,487 --> 00:01:16,294
Data saver lowers that to two; High quality
allows up to eight.

16
00:01:16,294 --> 00:01:21,088
Lower quality uses less data, which helps on a
mobile connection.

17
00:01:21,088 --> 00:01:27,299
Screen relay is subject to the service's
available allowance, shown on the Connection
page.

18
00:01:28,167 --> 00:01:30,567
Click Save and restart.

19
00:01:30,567 --> 00:01:34,523
Selecting Cloud relay alone does not activate
it.

20
00:01:34,523 --> 00:01:40,064
Wait for Voltura Air to reopen, then check the
relay status on Connection.

21
00:01:40,064 --> 00:01:45,644
Next, open Connect on the PC to pair your
device using the new relay route.

22
00:01:46,533 --> 00:01:53,121
On your phone, scan the current QR code from
the PC's Connect page and open the detected
link.

23
00:01:53,121 --> 00:01:57,979
Cloud relay opens the secure controller at
voltura dot S E.

24
00:01:57,979 --> 00:02:01,317
The code shown here is only a demonstration.

25
00:02:01,317 --> 00:02:05,840
Always scan your own PC's fresh code after
switching to Relay.

26
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:09,783
If it expires, choose New code and scan again.

27
00:02:10,667 --> 00:02:14,948
The controller asks you to confirm or edit your
device name.

28
00:02:14,948 --> 00:02:18,066
Tap Pair, then wait for the connection.

29
00:02:18,066 --> 00:02:21,559
Relay may take up to ten seconds to start.

30
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:24,471
The connected controller is shown here.

31
00:02:24,471 --> 00:02:32,615
Use this same browser or installed web app
later: it remembers the pairing unless its data
is cleared or the device is removed.

32
00:02:33,467 --> 00:02:38,521
Before leaving, open Devices on the PC and
select your paired device.

33
00:02:38,521 --> 00:02:41,769
Check that View PC screen is allowed.

34
00:02:41,769 --> 00:02:49,385
The Remote controls profile blocks screen
viewing; use the device's Custom permissions to
allow the access you need.

35
00:02:49,385 --> 00:02:53,998
Pointer and keyboard permission is also needed
to control the PC.

36
00:02:54,867 --> 00:02:59,225
Now try your phone on mobile data or another
internet connection.

37
00:02:59,225 --> 00:03:04,689
Reopen the same paired controller; keep its tab
or bookmark it after pairing.

38
00:03:04,689 --> 00:03:08,852
Choose your saved PC and Try reconnect if
prompted.

39
00:03:08,852 --> 00:03:14,109
Both devices need internet, but they no longer
need the same home network.

40
00:03:14,109 --> 00:03:18,207
An old Direct LAN bookmark is not the Relay
controller.

41
00:03:19,067 --> 00:03:23,825
On the connected device, open Menu and choose
View PC screen.

42
00:03:23,825 --> 00:03:26,595
Select the display you want to view.

43
00:03:26,595 --> 00:03:32,871
You can now see your Windows PC over the
internet while you're away from home or away
from the computer.

44
00:03:32,871 --> 00:03:38,760
The preview here uses a fictional desktop
inside the real Voltura Air interface.

45
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:46,156
Use the touch controls, or a mouse and keyboard
from another computer, with the required
permissions.

46
00:03:46,156 --> 00:03:50,576
Sound starts muted; enable it if you want PC
audio.

47
00:03:50,576 --> 00:03:53,875
One device can view a display at a time.

48
00:03:53,875 --> 00:03:57,161
Leave View PC screen to stop viewing.

49
00:03:57,161 --> 00:04:02,831
Commands, screen pixels, and PC audio remain
encrypted through the relay.

50
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:11,203
If the PC is unavailable, check that it's
awake, online, and still running Voltura Air in
Relay mode.

51
00:04:11,203 --> 00:04:16,009
Check internet or work-network restrictions,
then try reconnecting.

52
00:04:16,009 --> 00:04:19,734
A sleeping or shut-down PC cannot be reached.

53
00:04:19,734 --> 00:04:27,414
Pair and test before leaving, and find the
documentation and troubleshooting guide at
voltura.se/air.
